# Proton (arm64) — the compat tool that runs x86/x86-64 *Windows* games on this device.
#
# This is a community Proton build that ships an arm64-native Wine plus Valve's WoW64 FEX
# (files/lib/wine/aarch64-windows/libwow64fex.dll, libarm64ecfex.dll). The emulator translates
# only the game's x86 Windows code; every Linux syscall is made by the arm64 side of Wine. So
# this path is SELF-CONTAINED: it needs no system FEX package, no x86 guest rootfs, no thunks,
# and no Steam Linux Runtime container.
#
# Why bake it instead of letting Steam fetch a Proton:
#   - Valve's own arm64 Proton declares `require_tool_appid 4185400` (an arm64 SLR container).
#     On a non-Deckard client that tool is never *registered* even when its files are present,
#     so the launch dies before Proton runs. Baking a tool with no such dependency sidesteps the
#     platform gate entirely.
#   - Steam owns first-boot Wi-Fi, so nothing can be downloaded before OOBE completes. A baked
#     compat tool works on a device that has never been online.
#
# This tarball's own toolmanifest.vdf still carries `require_tool_appid`, and its compat-tool
# name is the versioned directory name. assemble-rootfs.sh rewrites both after extraction — see
# the compat-tool section there. Do not "fix" the manifest here; the tarball is upstream content
# and is extracted verbatim.
#
# strip: 1 + dest: the archive is rooted at the versioned directory
# (proton-cachyos-11.0-20260703-slr-arm64/), so stripping that component lands its CONTENTS
# directly in a stable, version-free directory name. NOTE the directory name is cosmetic: Steam
# pins a game to the tool's INTERNAL name (the compat_tools key inside compatibilitytool.vdf),
# not the directory — so assemble-rootfs.sh also rewrites that internal name to a stable id, or a
# bump would unpin every game regardless of the directory. See the compat-tool section there.
#
# The tool lives under /usr/share/steam/compatibilitytools.d, which the client does NOT scan on its
# own — novadeck-steam adds it via STEAM_EXTRA_COMPAT_TOOLS_PATHS. So it needs no seeding into $HOME
# and, unlike a copy under the user's Steam directory, it is replaced atomically with the OS slot
# and survives a factory reset.
#
# Upstream publishes a .sha512sum sidecar; the sha256 below was computed from the artifact.
#
# Fields: see packages/inputplumber/prebuilt.pin, plus `dest` (extraction root) documented in
# packages/fex-rootfs/prebuilt.pin.
#
# To bump: pick a release from https://github.com/CachyOS/proton-cachyos/releases carrying an
# `-arm64.tar.xz` asset, set version + url + sha256 together, and keep `dest` unchanged so games
# stay pinned to the same tool name. Re-verify the toolmanifest rewrite in assemble-rootfs.sh
# still matches (it fails loudly if upstream changes the commandline format).
name: proton-cachyos
version: 11.0-20260703-slr
url: https://github.com/CachyOS/proton-cachyos/releases/download/cachyos-11.0-20260703-slr/proton-cachyos-11.0-20260703-slr-arm64.tar.xz
sha256: 317f4b8f390fb4dea15ef9ebcf75cb4f350d01b61bff184fe29a1c4e10ce0cc5
kind: tar
strip: 1
dest: /usr/share/steam/compatibilitytools.d/proton-cachyos-11.0-arm64
# `proton` is a python3 script (#!/usr/bin/env python3); the wrapper that fronts it is python too.
deps: python
